sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Customer or agent
    participant P as Platform intake (web, MCP)
    participant S as Support desk (release gate)
    participant E as AI enclave
    actor Op as Operators
    C->>P: create_ticket(text, version, logs)
    P->>P: G1 entitlement + quota, G2 input guard
    alt rejected
        P-->>C: Canned reply
    else accepted (possibly flagged)
        P->>S: Store ticket, queue job
        S-->>C: Ticket id, status "analysing"
    end
    E->>S: Claim job (outbound pull)
    Note over E: Analyst: docs + source at the customer's release<br/>G3 bridge: schema only, no source text<br/>Responder: draft from public docs<br/>G4 output guard: secrets, fingerprint, grounding, policy
    E->>S: Finding (pointers), draft, guard report
    alt usage or config, confident, guards green, auto-send on
        S-->>C: Reply, marked as AI-generated
        S-)Op: Sent log entry
    else suspected bug or security issue
        S-)Op: Alert, internal finding, draft issue
        S-->>C: Templated acknowledgement
        Op->>S: Confirm or dismiss, reply
    else low confidence, guard flag or doc gap
        S-)Op: Review queue
        Op->>S: Approve, edit or reject
        S-->>C: Released reply
    end
